# Post-implementation Dart checks

After finishing any requested implementation (feature, fix, refactor, UI work), **before** considering the task done:

1. Run `dart format` on the paths you changed (or the project if many files).
2. Run `flutter analyze` (or `dart analyze` on touched packages) and fix errors/warnings you introduced.

Do not skip these steps even if the change looks trivial. Do not claim completion until both succeed (or remaining issues are pre-existing and called out).

```bash
# Prefer scoped format when possible
dart format lib/ path/to/changed.dart

flutter analyze
```

If analyze fails due to your changes, fix them in the same turn. Format-only diffs in unrelated files may be included when they result from this step.
